   = note: a buffer goes on an input, an output or a var (§5.1a)

error[SE0324]: a capacity on an input buffer
 --> tests/emit/lib/bufbad/BufBad.se:9:26
  |
9 |     inputs   { p: buffer(8); }                    // SE0324: a reader with a capacity
  |                          ^ a reader holds no bytes
  = note: an input reads the producer's storage, and a composite's port is a pass-through, so neither has a size of its own; it accepts any capacity (§5.1a)
  = help: write `p: buffer;`

error[SE0323]: buffer output `q` declares no capacity
  --> tests/emit/lib/bufbad/BufBad.se:10:19
